 "notes": "The catalogue names Śukadevabhaṭṭa as the scribe, which is wrong. The colophon says Sadāśiva jyotirvid, son of Rudra jyotirvid, copied the book ([li]khitaṃ … sadāśivajyotirvidā) for Śukadevabhaṭṭa (śukadevabhaṭṭanimittaṃ). Śukadevabhaṭṭa's lineage is traced back eight generations to Bhairavabhaṭṭa. 'Nāganātha' fills a lacuna (nā///ganātha), and the gap may have held more text. The era is not named ('saṃvat'). VS is assumed for a Devanagari North Indian manuscript, giving 1681 CE. The weekday was not checked. There is also a lacuna right after 'śane', which may have hidden more date or place details before '[li]khitaṃ'.",
